oing that so that's  number two listen a lot and repeatedly  to material easy material hopefully  where there's a lot of repetition of  vocabulary point number three  as soon as possible listen a lot again  to interesting material and remember  always try to have the transcript  available and the reason you want to  listen to interesting material is that  after a while our ability to absorb  things when we when we listen to things  that we've listened to before starts to  diminish so you have to mix in  interesting things where you're actually  interested in  what the subject matter is it might be a  novel it might be a story it might be  history you know sports whatever it is  that you're interested in so  make sure you have the transcript that's  number one  to listen a lot repeatedly to repetitive  somewhat less interesting material but  eventually and as much as possible and  as soon as possible move on to  interesting things that are going to  capture your curiosity so that you're  more focused on the  interest  this you know what it is they're talking  about  than  trying to focus in on words and phrases  and i find that  you know it doesn't matter what i'm  listening to there is a tendency to tune  out sitting in the car working out so  don't expect they're gonna always be 100  focused it doesn't matter you are  bathing your brain with the language  okay  fourth point is read read a lot okay not  only  things that you're listening to but all  reading  is tremendously valuable  in terms of giving you familiarity with  the language introducing vocabulary of  course until we have a large vocabulary  we have to read in my view in an  environment where it's like assisted  reading that's link so  you can look up words you can review the  words immediately after having read a  page at link but you have to read a lot  uh my statistics that link in terms of  the number of words that i have read  like even in greek  it's well in excess i don't know how  many hundred thousand words that i've  read just on link  you have to read a lot reading helps you  understand when you listen if you don't  have words if you don't have familiarity  with the language just listening  listening listening is not enough you  have to read a lot so that was the  fourth read a lot  now  again i mentioned this number five  variety vary the things that you're  listening to remember again we always  want to have that transcript available  until we're fairly advanced but try to  vary it variety is good for the brain  i don't mean three different things  within half an hour i mean focus on one  range of subject matter so you get some  familiarity with the context with the  vocabulary but then  at some other point  do something else and this can be as  simple as when you're starting out  having a variety of beginner material or  later on perhaps having two or three  different kinds of content history  literature whatever that you're  listening so  variety  is important so that's number five  number six  keep listening  don't say well i don't understand enough  keep listening in language learning  progress is slow and number seven keep  reading  there you have it  uh i won't remember all the seven but  the gist of it is keep doing it  vary it mixing the reading and listening  and eventually  your brain will start to focus and  there's no point being frustrated that  you  can't understand or you have trouble  focusing you just have to keep going  it's that simple okay then  that's all i have to say and now i'm  going to try to do a brief explanation  in greek as to why i'm moving on from  greek to arabic bye for now  you
 

